from pathlib import Path
import json,ast
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];source=R/'engine/animation/physical_proofs.py';tree=ast.parse(source.read_text());lines={n.name:n.lineno for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.FunctionDef)}
notes={'A':('Accelerator, 3 seconds','A seated hip/knee/ankle chain approaches the pedal. A rigid shoe reaches contact at .75 s, then rolls about a planted heel while the pedal rotates 24 degrees. The linked torso/shoulders/head load and settle; both hands remain on the wheel. Fixed camera, no cuts.','accelerator'), 'B':('Vehicle, 4 seconds','A metric arc-length path establishes a rolling start, smoothly accelerates from 2 to 7 m/s over 18 m, then releases load into a cruise hold and turns about 15 degrees. Wheels rotate by distance/radius, steering by curvature. Fixed-world houses, lamps and reflections share the projection. Camera follows only 65% of travel with partial pan: subject displacement remains visible. No HUD.','vehicle_state'), 'C':('Door and keys, 9 seconds','Extended from five seconds for readability; the final half second holds the completed entry. Reach, lever grip/turn, failed pull and torso recoil precede pocket retrieval, key alignment/insertion/rotation/withdrawal, handle regrip, hinge opening and supported entry. Targets constrain the hand to actual hardware. The exterior camera stays fixed; wall/leaf depth masks the entering owner.','door_state'), 'D':('Three stairs, 4 seconds','Metric 3D hip/knee/ankle chains solve against explicit treads, not a diagonally translated sprite. Foot lift occurs before forward swing; landing precedes pelvis transfer/extension. Toe-off rotates the shoe and attached ankle around a fixed forefoot. Three risers and a trailing-foot follow are completed. Fixed camera.','stair_state'), 'E':('Curtain/window, 4 seconds','Approach and arm reach precede a continuous grip. The curtain starts fully closed. Its edge follows the gripping hand; upper/lower folds lag. Planted feet and an actual sidestep support the pull; eyes lead silhouette-changing head rotation, torso recoil and fear. Grip release leaves damped fabric follow-through. Fixed camera.','curtain_state')}
for k,(title,explanation,fn) in notes.items():
 d=R/'proofs'/k;meta=json.loads((d/'final.json').read_text());filename=Path(meta['path']).name;d.joinpath('README.md').write_text(f'# {title}\n\n**[Play/download MP4]({filename}?raw=true)** · [Contact sheet](final_CONTACT_SHEET.jpg) · [Trajectory CSV](MOTION_TRAJECTORY.csv)\n\n{explanation}\n\nSource: [physical_proofs.py](../../engine/animation/physical_proofs.py#L{lines[fn]}), function `{fn}`; shared approved rig in [articulated.py](../../engine/animation/articulated.py). Preview and HD paths are recorded in `preview.json` and `final.json`.\n\nEvidence: `JOINTS_TRAJECTORIES.json`, `JOINT_TRANSFORMS.json`, `CONTACT_EVENTS.json`, `final_CONTACT_SHEET.jpg`, `final_PLAYBACK.json` and normal/half-speed presented-frame sheets. Videos are intentionally silent to expose motion.\n\nSee [numerical validation](../../reports/physical-proof-validation.json) and [integration gate](../../reports/proof-integration-gate.json). Technical validation is separate from user artistic approval.\n')
